From ea5a86cadf406cf98bb932c35d72661eca018d13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: autoresearch <agent@localhost>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:23:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] diar: pin attention_mask as a graph output too - it was
 being silently corrupted

rope_cos and rope_sin already carry both ggml_set_input AND ggml_set_output (needed so gallocr does not
recycle their buffer once the last layer consumes it), with a comment explaining why. attention_mask never
got the second call - an oversight, not a deliberate choice, since the comment at the read-back site claims
all three "are graph INPUTS, so they are materialised in the backend buffer and can simply be read back",
which is only true for the two that also carry the output flag.

Found while resuming the one-runtime-merge port (docs/one-runtime-merge.md): the port's flash_attn_ext was
producing 100% non-finite output for every axis-convention variant, which looked like a Q/K/V layout bug.
Dumping AUDIOCPP_DUMP_LAYER0's own layer0_mask.f16 and inspecting it directly showed it was not a mask at
all - 2301 of 152881 elements NaN, 6 Inf, values up to +-65000, and only 2739 real zeros where a session with
no padding should be all zeros. The values cluster near -2.0 with activation-like precision, consistent with
a later layer's normalized hidden state having been allocated over the mask's freed buffer by the time the
dump read it back. Feeding that garbage mask into flash attention is sufficient on its own to produce the
NaN the port was chasing.

With this pinned, a fresh AUDIOCPP_DUMP_LAYER0 dump's mask is clean (single unique value 0.0 on a
window with no padding), and the port's flash attention output is finite. Also newly visible: 02_qkv,
07_oproj and 11_ffn_out remain corrupted in the SAME way despite already being ggml_set_output (07_oproj and
11_ffn_out read back the identical rms to many digits, i.e. two different tensors sharing one recycled
address) - marking a tensor as a graph output does not protect it from a later layer's structurally
identical tensor landing on the same gallocr slot. That confirms docs/one-runtime-merge.md's own conclusion
that traced intermediates from the running 32-layer graph cannot be a sound oracle; only layer0_in, the now-
fixed mask/rope tables, and a layer built in true isolation can be trusted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QJVEwbN82WXJr6Us6kowEX
---
 src/models/nemotron_3_diar/encoder.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/models/nemotron_3_diar/encoder.cpp b/src/models/nemotron_3_diar/encoder.cpp
index 67424c9..0826e31 100644
--- a/src/models/nemotron_3_diar/encoder.cpp
+++ b/src/models/nemotron_3_diar/encoder.cpp
@@ -290,7 +290,13 @@ void ensure_encoder_graph(
     next->probabilities = modules::SigmoidModule().build(ctx, output);
     ggml_set_input(next->input.tensor);
     ggml_set_input(next->attention_mask.tensor);
-    // These tables are populated once and must survive every graph execution.
+    // These tables are populated once and must survive every graph execution. attention_mask needs the same
+    // ggml_set_output pin as rope_cos/rope_sin - set_input alone does not stop gallocr from recycling its
+    // buffer once the last layer consumes it, so a later read (the layer0 dump, or a second window reusing
+    // the same persistent tensor) can return whatever node was allocated on top of it. Without this line the
+    // dumped mask was garbage (2301/152881 NaN, values up to +-65000, only 2739 real zeros) - not a real
+    // 0/-10000 validity mask at all - which is why every downstream layer0_port comparison saw NaN.
+    ggml_set_output(next->attention_mask.tensor);
     ggml_set_input(next->rope_cos.tensor);
     ggml_set_input(next->rope_sin.tensor);
     ggml_set_output(next->rope_cos.tensor);
